      "writtenOn": "2023-10-24T12:15:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For this new LOCAL_NETWORK capability, can we be totally opinionated and simply just ignore any attempt to change its value on an existing network? I think the lesson from the code above is that the WTF doesn\u0027t really prevent this from happening, and many callers of this code believe that changing immutable capabilities is supported.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 8823,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 8823,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "f88210634d5658f9f0108e7193d100dd6e8b774e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "98748403_5aa4cfdf",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java",
        "patchSetId": 21
      },
      "lineNbr": 8823,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-31T12:19:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we should be even more opinionated than this, possibly going as far as crashing the system server for a bad agent.\n\nPer offline discussion, aosp/2805415 implements disconnecting the agent if it sends a bad update.",
      "parentUuid": "98f244ac_5bc772c2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 8823,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 8823,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "f88210634d5658f9f0108e7193d100dd6e8b774e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
