      "writtenOn": "2023-12-08T07:53:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In addition to the capabilities, NetworkRequest has other fields, such as the request ID and legacy type. In particular, what happens looks like if the factory sends an upstreamSelector with a given capabilities, but then sends another request with a new upstreamSelector that has the same capabilities but a different legacyType or requestId? Perhaps it doesn\u0027t matter because the NetworkRequest passed in by the factory is ignored, and we construct a new NetworkRequest here in line 9034?",
